7,-0.21277783811092377,-0.03375734016299248,-4.768370445162873e-07,-0.339402437210083,-1.0461039543151855,-0.17282474040985107,-8.034383063204587e-05,-0.0008108903421089053,-0.6157547235488892,-0.019853563979268074,-0.0004913791781291366,-0.00023135847004596144,-0.13606634736061096,-8.22540732769994e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-4.458328112377785e-05,-1.3677115440368652,-8.4638240878121e-06,-0.00011431517486926168,-0.007609074469655752,-0.0015307862777262926,-0.2731899619102478,-0.0013080621138215065,-0.10073821246623993,-0.0003277718205936253,-0.0123963113874197,-0.023377282544970512,-0.06102564558386803,-0.3047749996185303,-0.04813788831233978,-0.3909437954425812,-0.0009108209051191807,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.005700521636754274,-2.634490556374658e-05,-0.0776142030954361,-0.7917094230651855,-0.842849612236023,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.0009734659106470644,-0.6674221158027649,0.0,-9.703165414975956e-05,-0.010145050473511219,0.0,-0.00037901371251791716,-1.1920922133867862e-06,-0.00014304091746453196,-5.054346183896996e-05],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,69,2075,15087,387,264,729,1741,429,369,678,400,87,4779,400,69,2075,8,284,282,2075,488,220,16,8,488,282,2075,481,220,16,568,3,220,16246,429,400,69,7,16,20,8,284,220,17,15,3,323,400,69,7,17,15,8,284,220,16,20,4779,12564,400,69,7,17,15,16,20,17,15,16,20,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f(x)$ be a function such that for all $x,$ $f(x) = f(x + 1) + f(x - 1).$  Given that $f(15) = 20$ and $f(20) = 15,$ compute $f(20152015).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3a06947d31691cba40d873bfa71381aed6cb94523de23cfa4a624a1607c9fd49"},"seconds":57.51891803741455,"seed":209512947924771505,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( f(20152015) \\), we need to understand the behavior of the function \\( f(x) \\) given the functional equation \\( f(x) = f(x+1) + f(x-1) \\).\n\nFirst, let's explore the functional equation by expressing a few terms in terms of others. Consider \\( f(x+1) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+1) = f(x+2) + f(x)\n\\]\nFrom the original equation, we have:\n\\[\nf(x) = f(x+1) + f(x-1)\n\\]\nSubstitute \\( f(x+1) \\) from the first equation into the second:\n\\[\nf(x) = (f(x+2) + f(x)) + f(x-1)\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\nf(x) = f(x+2) + f(x) + f(x-1)\n\\]\nSubtract \\( f(x) \\) from both sides:\n\\[\n0 = f(x+2) + f(x-1)\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nf(x+2) = -f(x-1)\n\\]\n\nNext, let's find a general pattern by evaluating more terms. Consider \\( f(x+2) \\) and \\( f(x-1) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+3) = f(x+4) + f(x+2)\n\\]\nUsing \\( f(x+2) = -f(x-1) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+3) = f(x+4) - f(x-1)\n\\]\nAlso, from the original equation:\n\\[\nf(x+2) = f(x+3) + f(x+1)\n\\]\nSubstitute \\( f(x+3) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+2) = (f(x+4) - f(x-1)) + f(x+1)\n\\]\nUsing \\( f(x+2) = -f(x-1) \\):\n\\[\n-f(x-1) = f(x+4) - f(x-1) + f(x+1)\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n0 = f(x+4) + f(x+1)\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nf(x+4) = -f(x+1)\n\\]\n\nWe now have a recurrence relation:\n\\[\nf(x+4) = -f(x+1)\n\\]\n\nTo find a periodic pattern, let's evaluate \\( f(x+8) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+8) = f((x+4)+4) = -f((x+4)+1) = -f(x+5)\n\\]\nUsing \\( f(x+4) = -f(x+1) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+5) = f(x+4+1) = -f(x+1+1) = -f(x+2)\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nf(x+8) = -(-f(x+2)) = f(x+2)\n\\]\nSince \\( f(x+2) = -f(x-1) \\):\n\\[\nf(x+8) = f(x-1)\n\\]\n\nWe observe that \\( f(x) \\) is periodic with period 8. Thus:\n\\[\nf(x+8k) = f(x)\n\\]\n\nGiven \\( f(15) = 20 \\) and \\( f(20) = 15 \\), we can use the periodicity:\n\\[\n20152015 \\mod 8 = 7\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nf(20152015) = f(7)\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( f(7) \\), we use the periodicity and the given values:\n\\[\nf(7) = f(-1)\n\\]\nFrom the functional equation:\n\\[\nf(0) = f(1) + f(-1)\n\\]\nUsing \\( f(4) = -f(1) \\):\n\\[\nf(4) = -f(1)\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\nf(8) = -f(5) = f(1)\n\\]\nGiven \\( f(15) = 20 \\):\n\\[\nf(15) = f(7) = 20\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{20}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
